@ [at sign, Method Debugger]
The cell @ in the column Name shows the identifier of the active MU, i.e., the MU that triggers the call of
the current Method in a control. You cannot change the contents of the cell!
Remarks
Press F2 to open the dialog box of the MU. If a user-defined method contains the identifier @ and if you
would like to test the Method without running the simulation, you have to specify a suitable object in the
object Method. The Debugger uses the contents of the cell @ of the Method.
The Watch Window shows changed values in red in the cells under Value.
See also
Anonymous Identifiers > @ [SimTalk] - anonymous identifier
@ [at sign, Method Debugger]
11-3676 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

? [question mark, Method Debugger]
The cell ? in the column Name shows the name of the object that calls the Method.
Remarks
If that is another Method, the cell contains the name of that Method. Otherwise, it contains the name of
the object in which a MU triggered a control call. You cannot change the contents of the cell!
Press F2 to open the dialog box of the calling object. If a user-defined Method contains the identifier ? and
you would like to test the Method without running the simulation, you have to specify a suitable object in
the object Method. The Debugger uses the contents of the cell ? of the Method.
The Watch Window shows changed values in red in the cells under Value.
See also
Anonymous Identifiers [described] > ? [SimTalk] - anonymous identifier
Tab Call Stack [Watch window]
Shows the sequence in which the Methods are called, i.e., the call chain. The first Method to be activated
is always located at the bottom of the list, while the top line shows the Method being executed at the
moment.
? [question mark, Method Debugger]
Plant Simulation Help 11-3677
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Remarks
Double-click a cell on the tab Call Stack to open the respective Method, together with its current settings
of local variables and parameters, in the Debugger. Double-click the topmost cell to return to the Method
being executed at the moment.
The column Method shows the name of the Method.
The column Parameters shows the parameters of the Method.
Note
The column always shows the current value of the parameters, i.e., if the value was changed in the
meantime, the new value is shown, not the value that was originally passed to the Method.
SimTalk
getCallStack [SimTalk]
