Tab Call Chains [Watch window]
Shows Methods which are ready to be executed immediately.
Remarks
Do not confuse these with the active Method being executed at the moment.
11-3678 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Active Methods are methods that were called and are now waiting to be executed while other Methods,
such as other controls triggered by events, are still being executed.
Video on YouTube
https://youtu.be/5t-wLNmKpbU?si=A_B8xFC_7MKVPVu1&t=552
Tab Suspended [Watch window]
Shows Methods that were suspended by a waituntil-statement or by a stopuntil-statement.
Remarks
The Tab Suspended also shows Methods, which have been suspended by a wait-instruction or by a sleep
[SimTalk]-instruction.
The caller of the Method is displayed in parentheses, preceded by the absolute Path. Double-click an entry
to change to that Method. The third column shows the statement which suspended the Method.
If you add a comment after a waituntil-statement, a stopuntil-statement, a wait-statement, or a sleep-
statement to the source code of your Method and if this comment starts with three hyphens --- or with
three forward slashes ///, Plant Simulation does not show the entire statement on the Tab Suspended of
the Watch Window and of the Method Debugger, but only the comment.
Video on YouTube
Plant Simulation Help 11-3679
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

The method deleteSuspendedMethods deletes all suspensions of all methods.
Plant Simulation shows as tooltip in the Frame window.
The tooltip shows the caller of the method, in our case the ExitContr, and the suspended instruction, in
our case waituntil SP.empty prio @.ID wait 5:00 ? = PP, which is suspended three times.
