Tab Expressions [Watch window]
Type in any kind of expression which the Debugger is going to evaluate on the tab Expressions.
Remarks
Double-click a row in the list, type in an expression, for example self.xPos+1, and click OK, so that Plant
Simulation applies this entry.
You will notice that the Debugger shows self.xPos+1 in the column Expression and current value in the
column Value. If you select Show Expression for all Methods, Plant Simulation shows this expression in
the dialog of all Methods.
You can edit the contents of the tab Expressions on the tab itself. To open a variable or an expression
whose value has the data type object, click in the cell and press F2. If the tab Expressions shows a local
variable or an attribute, you can edit its value in the cells in the column Value.
Note
The tab Expressions is not available if the Method is executed as a formula.
Video on YouTube
https://youtu.be/5t-wLNmKpbU?si=A_B8xFC_7MKVPVu1&t=552
