Toolbar of the Method Debugger
The toolbar of the Method Debugger provides buttons with commands helping you to debug your
methods.
To do this Click Menu command, SimTalk
Open the location of the Method, i.e., the Frame in which the
Method is located.
Open Location, Location
[SimTalk] - material flow
objects
Open the origin of the Method from which the active Method was
derived.
Open Origin, Origin
Return the Debugger to the currently executed Method.
 —
Open the Watch Window.
 Watch Window
Execute one line of the debugged Method at a time. Any methods
being called in that line of the source code will not be loaded.
Step Over
Execute one line of the debugged Method at a time. If that line of
the source code happens to call other Methods, these are loaded
as well.
Step Into
Step out of the current Method and move on to beginning of the
next statement in the calling Method.
Step Out
Continue executing the active Method.
 Continue
Stop the simulation, i.e., stop the execution of all active Methods.
 Terminate Simulation
Insert a breakpoint into the class or remove it from it.
 Class Breakpoint
Insert a breakpoint into the instance or remove it from it.
 Instance Breakpoint
Delete all breakpoints in the Method.
 Remove All Breakpoints ,
clearAllBreakpoints
[SimTalk]
Temporarily activate or deactivate the animation of the moving
objects and object states. Plant Simulation restores the original
setting as soon as you close the Debugger window.
MU and State Animation
