Continue [method execution]
Continues executing the active Method.
Or you can click 
  on the Toolbar of the Method Debugger
.
Run to Cursor
Continues executing the Method until it reaches the statement at which the cursor is located.
Remarks
The Method Debugger shows the elapsed time if you execute one or several instructions in a Method with
the commands Step Over, Step Into, Step Out, or Run to Cursor and if executing the instructions takes
10 milliseconds or longer.
Video on YouTube
Plant Simulation Help 11-3691
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Set Next Statement
Sets the next statement that is going to be executed.
Remarks
Click Yes in the dialog that opens to continue executing the current Method in the line in which the cursor
is located.
Click No if you do not want this and to return to the current position of the cursor.
Let us illustrate this with an example: Suppose a Method is caught in an endless loop. To get out of this,
hold down the Shift+Ctrl+Alt keys to stop method execution, and set the cursor outside of the loop.
Then, press Ctrl+F10 to get out of the loop and press F5 to continue executing the Method.
Note
The feature Set Next Statement provides the same function as Ctrl+double-clicking the left mouse
button.
Return From Current Call Chain
Terminates the entire call chain which was invoked to start the current Method. The simulation run will
continue afterward.
Set Next Statement
11-3692 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Terminate Simulation
Terminates all call chains, i.e., the current and all other call chains pointing to waiting methods, and stops
the simulation.
Or click 
  on the Toolbar of the Method Debugger
.
Restart Simulation
Starts the simulation again after you stopped it.
Remarks
Restart Simulation does the same as clicking Reset Simulation and then clicking Start/Stop Simulation
in the EventController does, i.e., it terminates the active simulation run and resets and starts the
simulation again.
Class Breakpoint
Inserts a breakpoint into the class of the source code or removes it from it.
Remarks
The command is described under Toggle Class Breakpoint.
To insert a class breakpoint, you can also click 
  on the Toolbar of the Method Debugger
.
Terminate Simulation
Plant Simulation Help 11-3693
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Instance Breakpoint
Adds an instance breakpoint to this instance of the source code or deletes it.
Instance Breakpoint Command
The command is described under Toggle Instance Breakpoint.
To insert an instance breakpoint, you can also click 
  on the Toolbar of the Method Debugger
.
